1.SMALLER AND LARGER IN SORTED
Given a sorted array arr[] and a value target, return an array of size 2. The first value is the number of elements less than or equal to the target, and the second value is the number of elements greater than or equal to the target.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int[] getMoreAndLess(int[] arr, int target) {
                int less=0,great=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]<=target){
                        less++;
                    }
                    if(arr[i]>=target){
                        great++;
                    }
                }
                return new int[]{less,great};
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/smaller-and-larger4005/1


2.REVERSE AN ARRAY
You are given an array of integers arr[]. You have to reverse the given array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public void reverseArray(int arr[]) {
                int i=0;
                int j=arr.length-1;
                int temp;
                while(i<j){
                    temp=arr[i];
                    arr[i]=arr[j];
                    arr[j]=temp;
                    j--;
                    i++;
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/reverse-an-array/1


3.COUNT THE ZEROS
Given an array arr of only 0's and 1's. The array is sorted in such a manner that all the 1's are placed first and then they are followed by all the 0's. Find the count of all the 0's.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int countZeroes(int[] arr) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                int count=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]==0){
                        count++;
                    }
                }
                return count;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/count-the-zeros2550/1


4.PRIME NUMBERS
Given a number n, determine whether it is a prime number or not.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static boolean isPrime(int n) {
                if(n<2){
                    return false;
                }
                int count=0;
                for(int i=2;i<=Math.sqrt(n);i++){
                    if(n%i==0){
                        count++;
                    }
                }
                return count==0;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/prime-number2314/1


5.FIRST OCCURRENCE IN SORTED
Given a sorted array arr[] and an integer k, find the position(0-based indexing) at which k is present in the array using binary search. If k doesn't exist in arr[] return -1.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int firstSearch(int[] arr, int k) {
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]==k){
                        return i;
                    }
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
