6.MOVE ALL ZEROES TO END
You are given an array arr[] of non-negative integers. You have to move all the zeros in the array to the right end while maintaining the relative order of the non-zero elements. 
The operation must be performed in place, meaning you should not use extra space for another array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            void pushZerosToEnd(int[] arr) {
                int j=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]!=0){
                        int temp=arr[i];
                        arr[i]=arr[j];
                        arr[j]=temp;
                        j++;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/move-all-zeroes-to-end-of-array0751/1
